{"id": "EUVD-2026-103547", "enisaUuid": "86e2ae54-9713-323b-bc22-126f29ad8bd7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btnxpuart: Fix skb leak in nxp_process_fw_dump()\n\nWhen CONFIG_DEV_COREDUMP=n, hci_devcd_append() returns -EOPNOTSUPP\nwithout freeing its skb argument. This leaks the cloned skb and also\nprevents nxp_set_ind_reset() from being called to perform recovery.\n\nFix by guarding the hci_devcd_append(hdev, skb_clone(skb, GFP_ATOMIC))\ncall with IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DEV_COREDUMP).", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a36598050cd1e5abb1d5ed42cc224cfcb538c4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edcb84ee607a9ddfc6f2771a7f399115f0b0f19d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2bbb36426581045a8bf7793da5419b9375e4348"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xvhg-mjvc-rxvr", "CVE-2026-98633"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "184e6fd7-2148-3306-9de6-919221d47826", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "2d3fa594-f06e-31cd-8493-c1636bb15b81", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "419ebe1e-fd83-36d2-9245-dd438295a0e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "44b15d70-5271-3cae-a67a-4ff4de11b1fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "998e447f443f138c90faa6ff3845082af419070e <f2bbb36426581045a8bf7793da5419b9375e4348"}, {"id": "8ec8cbcc-02ea-396d-a5cd-0c04c0a4d239", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "998e447f443f138c90faa6ff3845082af419070e <8a36598050cd1e5abb1d5ed42cc224cfcb538c4f"}, {"id": "b0adc020-fede-3a30-bc98-aa27eb4076c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "dc8a